Game of Drones: the game CodinGame runs today, drawn from the seed. "Referees/Game of Drones/Referee.java" of
https://github.com/SpiritusSancti5/codinGame (c0cc6fe) is CodinGame's referee without a base class (its main runs
`new Referee().start(System.in)`); this patch makes two changes, nothing else:

1. The seed. With no init line the referee draws its game from `new Random(System.currentTimeMillis())` (the drone count
   3 + 2 * nextInt(5), then the zones and the drones; nbZones = 2 x the players); with init lines it expects exactly
   three, "nbZones=", "nbDrones=" and "gameSeed=" (its UINPUT, to replay a game). The jar's CLI (referees/cg-builder/
   legacy) passes the single init line "seed=N": the file takes it for the three-line form and fails at once (an
   ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException caught as an invalid input: no game, every score 0). Here one "seed=N" line is the
   first path seeded with N (`new Random(N)` instead of the clock); no line and the three-line form are unchanged. The
   UINPUT (the jar's game parameters) is then "nbZones=<2 x players>", "nbDrones=<3..11>", "gameSeed=N".
   CodinGame's games are this path: in 587 replays of its top two leagues (gameResult/findByGameId: 114 games of 2
   players, 186 of 3, 287 of 4) the referee input is "nbZones=<2 x players>", "nbDrones=<3 + 2 x Random(gameSeed).
   nextInt(5)>", "gameSeed=<a clock time in ms>": the seed decides the whole game, and "-seed <gameSeed>" replays it.

2. The zones (the rule of CodinGame's live referee, inferred from its replays). The file draws each zone (x in
   [100, 3550), y in [350, 1700)) until it is at least 700 from every zone before it; with 8 zones (4 players) this may
   take very long or never end (the zones already placed can leave no room: the jar then loops forever and the game
   fails). CodinGame's zones are the file's in 584 of the 587 replays; the other three (4 players) are the zones of
   this rule: after 501 failed draws in a row for one zone, the zones are drawn again from zone 1 on (zone 0 kept, the
   draws go on). Searched among per-zone and global failure counters, restarting from zone 0 or 1, for every limit
   from 480 to 520: only this one, with exactly 501, gives CodinGame's zones in all 587 replays; the jar built with it
   reproduces every frame of the 587 replays (views, infos, summaries, who plays, game parameters, scores) from
   "seed=<gameSeed>", the file's own rule 584 (scratchpad cg-2014-game-of-drones/scripts/replay_check.py, zone_rules.py).

Applied by legacy/build.sh for the output name cg-2014-game-of-drones. The file with change 1 only (no zone rule) is
built as cg-2014-game-of-drones-original (patches/cg-2014-game-of-drones-original.patch).

